@@ -200,6 +200,35 @@ The following arguments are supported:
 
 The middleware won't GZip responses that already have a `Content-Encoding` set, to prevent them from being encoded twice.
 
+## RequestBodyLimitMiddleware
+
+Buffers HTTP request bodies before calling the application and rejects bodies
+larger than `max_bytes`. The limit counts bytes received, regardless of the
+`Content-Length` header. On the first crossing, the middleware stops reading and
+returns a plain-text `413` response with the body `Request body too large`, without
+calling the application. Accepted bodies are replayed to the application so that
+request body and JSON helpers work as usual. Subsequent receives are delegated to
+the original receive stream, including disconnect events.
+
+```python
+from starlette.applications import Starlette
+from starlette.middleware import Middleware
+from starlette.middleware.body_limit import RequestBodyLimitMiddleware
+
+routes = ...
+
+app = Starlette(
+    routes=routes,
+    middleware=[Middleware(RequestBodyLimitMiddleware, max_bytes=1024 * 1024)],
+)
+```
+
+`max_bytes` must be `None` or a non-negative integer. Invalid values, including
+booleans, raise `ValueError` when the middleware is constructed. A zero limit
+accepts empty bodies, and bodies exactly at the limit are allowed. `None` disables
+both buffering and the limit. WebSocket and lifespan scopes pass through without
+buffering.
+
 ## BaseHTTPMiddleware
 
 An abstract class that allows you to write ASGI middleware against a request/response
